<title>BELGIUM: Vets to hold special swine fever meeting on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Vets to hold special swine fever meeting on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's Standing Veterinary Committee will hold a special meeting on Wednesday to discuss the worsening swine fever situation, a Commission official said.</p>
<p>The official, speaking on Friday, noted that the veterinary committee earlier this week supported a partial ban on exports of pigs from six German states after an outbreak of swine fever.</p>
<p>The ban is due to be formally approved by the Commission on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Belgium and Switzerland have announced curbs on imports of live pigs and pork meat from Germany.</p>
<p>On Friday, the Dutch Agriculture Ministry said it had detected two new cases of swine fever, taking the number of affected farms to four, and confirmed that Poland had banned the import of pigs from the Netherlands.</p>
